        "Study_Objective": "Evaluate workability, compressive, splitting tensile, flexural and long-term strength of concrete with steel slag replacing 10-20% cement, 25-100% sand or 25-100% gravel (w/c 0.45).",
        "Abstract_or_Key_Finding": "Cement replacement reduced 28 d strength (28.02-33.20 vs 35.41 MPa); 20% best among cement mixes. 25% sand replacement raised strength to 36.93 MPa; 50% gravel replacement gave 41.61 MPa and highest flexural 7.23 MPa. Slag reduced slump in all cases. 10% cement mix improved with age but stayed below control at 180 d.",
